    {
      "id": "claim_013f489f33794819ad784a6cb232b3a4",
      "statement": "promote-release.ts publishes a candidate by copying candidates/<id>/manifest.json to releases/<id>/manifest.json — one all-or-nothing copy — but the copy is not isolated against concurrency, so callers must serialize promote runs; exit-0 guards cover already-promoted re-runs and candidates superseded by a higher CI run number (promoting an older candidate after a newer release shipped would roll production back), and a missing candidate manifest is a hard error.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/release/promote-release.ts#L1-L33",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:09013d821fff49f001cc021971d1d74916093f0d75a24906d474b4d4d094d7ed:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_74635434ca55422490db4b614a298411",
      "statement": "The release manifest is the contract between CI and the deploy service: it parses each package's wrangler.jsonc and emits binding templates with account-specific values replaced by a closed set of placeholders ($ACCOUNT_ID, $KV_<BINDING>_ID, $R2_<BINDING>_NAME, $WORKER_NAME(<pkg>), $SECRET(<name>), $PUBLIC_BASE_URL); the deploy-side renderer fails on unrecognized $ tokens and MANIFEST_VERSION guards co-evolution.",
      "evidence": [
